@startuml socket_login
title Socket — Login & Message Flow

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA

actor Client

participant "Client\n(base class)" as CB
participant "ClientSocket\n(doLogin)" as CS
participant "ServerSocket" as SS
participant "ClientHandlerSocket" as CHS
participant "ClientMessageVisitorImpl" as CMV
participant "ServerMessageVisitorImpl" as SMV
participant "MatchManager" as MM

note over CB, CS
  Client.login() is defined in the abstract base class.
  ClientSocket.doLogin() is the transport-specific implementation
  called after validation passes.
end note

== Connection ==

Client -> CS : connect(host, port)
CS -> SS : TCP handshake
SS -> CHS : new ClientHandlerSocket(socket, matchManager)
note right of CHS
  Constructor internally creates a first
  ClientMessageVisitorImpl (visitor field).
  It will be overwritten by setVisitor() below.
end note
SS -> SS : new ClientMessageVisitorImpl(matchManager, handler)
SS -> CHS : handler.setVisitor(visitor)
SS -> CHS : pool.submit(handler)

== Stream Init (run()) ==

CHS -> CHS : setup()\n→ ObjectOutputStream\n→ ObjectInputStream\n[enters readObject() loop]

== Login — Success ==

Client -> CB : login(nickname)
CB -> CB : check: nickname null/blank?\n→ no: proceed
CB -> CS : doLogin(nickname)
CS -> CS : vm.setNickname(nickname)\nloginFuture = new CompletableFuture<>()
CS -> CHS : [TCP] LoginMessage(nickname)
note over CS
  doLogin() now blocks on loginFuture.get(),
  waiting for the reader thread to complete it
  via onLoginSuccess() or onLoginFailed().
end note

CHS -> CHS : readObject() → onClientMessage(msg)\nmsg.accept(visitor)
CHS -> CMV : visit(LoginMessage)
CMV -> MM : login(nickname, clientHandler)
MM --> CMV : [no exception]
CMV -> CHS : onLogin(nickname)
CHS -> CHS : this.nickname = nickname\nthis.lastMessageReceivedTime = now\nstartHealthCheck()
CMV -> CHS : onLoginSuccess(nickname)
CHS -> CS : [TCP] LoginSuccessMessage(nickname)

note over CS
  Reader thread receives LoginSuccessMessage
  and dispatches to ServerMessageVisitorImpl.
end note
CS -> SMV : visit(LoginSuccessMessage)
SMV -> CS : clientSocket.onLoginSuccess()
CS -> CS : loginFuture.complete(true)\nsocket.setSoTimeout(PING_TIMEOUT)
SMV -> SMV : if (!clientSocket.isInGame())\n→ ui.onLogin(nickname)
note over CS
  loginFuture.get() unblocks → doLogin() returns true.
end note
CS --> CB : true
CB --> Client : true

== Login — Alt: Empty/Null Nickname ==

Client -> CB : login(nickname)
CB -> CB : check: nickname null/blank?\n→ yes: ui.printError(new InvalidUsernameException("Il nickname non può essere vuoto."))\nreturn false (without sending LoginMessage)
CB --> Client : false

== Login — Alt: InvalidUsernameException ==

Client -> CB : login(nickname)
CB -> CB : check: nickname null/blank?\n→ no: proceed
CB -> CS : doLogin(nickname)
CS -> CS : vm.setNickname(nickname)\nloginFuture = new CompletableFuture<>()
CS -> CHS : [TCP] LoginMessage(nickname)
note over CS
  doLogin() blocks on loginFuture.get().
end note

CHS -> CHS : readObject() → onClientMessage(msg)\nmsg.accept(visitor)
CHS -> CMV : visit(LoginMessage)
CMV -> MM : login(nickname, clientHandler)
note right of MM
  nickname already registered → InvalidUsernameException("Username già esistente nella lobby, inserire un nuovo username")
  (null/blank check already done in Client.login(),
  but MatchManager re-checks as server-side defence)
end note
MM --> CMV : throws InvalidUsernameException
CMV -> CHS : onLoginFailed(e.getMessage())
CHS -> CS : [TCP] LoginFailedMessage(errorMsg)

CS -> SMV : visit(LoginFailedMessage)
SMV -> SMV : ui.printError(new InvalidUsernameException(message.getError()))
SMV -> CS : clientSocket.onLoginFailed()
CS -> CS : loginFuture.complete(false)
note over CS
  loginFuture.get() unblocks → doLogin() returns false.
end note
CS --> CB : false
CB --> Client : false

@enduml